\title{Metadata nodes and the \code{\verb~|nondep~} flag of \code{\verb~|let~} are part of the official term identity}
\taxon{Insight}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{soundness}
\tag{loader}
\tag{store}
\tag{reference-engine}
\meta{origin}{docs/design/review/reference-caches.md}
\meta{updated}{2026-11-24}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Source: [the audit of the reference engine's caches](rep-reference-caches), sections 0 and 1, findings S3-F2 and R2-F1; [the exactness session](ses-874D). The audit compared, part by part, what the official caches take for the same term with what the loader and the store keep.}
\table{
\tr{\th{Part of a term}\th{Official equality}\th{RLVM}\th{Same}}
\tr{\td{binder name and binder info}\td{ignored}\td{not stored}\td{yes}}
\tr{\td{two records with one content}\td{one key}\td{one id}\td{yes}}
\tr{\td{universe levels}\td{by spelling}\td{interned structurally, no normal form at load}\td{yes}}
\tr{\td{Nat and String literals}\td{by value}\td{by value}\td{yes}}
\tr{\td{a metadata node}\td{part of the term}\td{dropped by the loader}\td{no}}
\tr{\td{the \code{\verb~|nondep~} flag of \code{\verb~|let~}}\td{part of the term, not in the hash}\td{not stored}\td{no}}
\tr{\td{which object a term is}\td{seen by pointer tests}\td{not represented}\td{no}}
}
\ul{
\li{The finding that started the audit was a wrong accept of the reference engine, the oracle of every gate, and it was not a kernel cache: the loader drops metadata records, so the wrapped expression stands for the node.}
\li{Officially a metadata node is a term of its own for every cache and hides what is under it from the syntactic tests of the kernel.}
\li{The \code{\verb~|nondep~} flag is the same class: \code{\verb~|r2-id-let-nondep-bad~} is rejected officially and accepted by the reference engine.}
\li{Both findings are of the tolerated kind. In the strict mode the loader declines a declaration that carries a metadata node, and since the evening of 2026-11-24 also one that carries a let with the flag \code{\verb~|nondep~}; when this was first written that decline was not yet published.}
\li{The other direction, a rejection of what the official checker accepts, is not tolerated. Two mechanisms were found, both a syntactic test of the official kernel that stops at a node: the test for eager reduction, and the cheap beta reduction of an inferred type together with the cache of successful pairs, see [the example](ex-FD6K). Both are closed since the evening of 2026-11-24, see [the decision](dec-7UAL).}
}
\transclude{ex-4B5D}
\p{Everything else that decides what "the same term" is agrees with the official kernel. The third row marked "no" is [object identity](ins-E3MS).}
\p{See also: [the caches of the reference engine](design-reference-caches); [the term store](design-term-store).}
